cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this formalization in research, please cite the specific
  archived release of TruncatedSieveFlux.
type: software
title: "TruncatedSieveFlux: Lean 4 Formalization of Finite Möbius Sieve Identities and Periodic Rounding-Error Moments"
authors:
  - family-names: Odasso
    given-names: Alessandro
abstract: >-
  Experimental AI-assisted mathematical formalization in Lean 4 and Mathlib,
  initiated and maintained by Alessandro Odasso, a non-mathematician exploring
  the use of large language models in scientific research. OpenAI GPT-6 series
  carried out substantial mathematical exploration, proof construction,
  debugging and verification work under human direction. The repository
  contains finite Möbius sieve identities, a logarithmic-cutoff residual
  bound, exact modular covariance and second-moment identities, and
  fourth-moment inequalities. Completed Lean proofs compile, and selected
  claims have documented Comparator checks. The human experimenter cannot
  independently guarantee mathematical correctness, originality or significance;
  independent mathematical review is invited. Stronger fourth-moment
  estimates remain unproved.
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexodas/TruncatedSieveFlux"
url: "https://github.com/alexodas/TruncatedSieveFlux"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - Möbius function
  - sieve theory
  - number theory
  - periodic rounding errors
  - research software
